From: Nerves KickPi K2B <nerves@kickpi-k2b>
Subject: [PATCH] allwinner: reload the watchdog counter on system reset

The native PSCI SYSTEM_RESET handler armed the watchdog by writing the
config and mode registers but never reloaded the counter. On H616/H618
enabling the mode register alone does not start the countdown, so the
watchdog never fired: the handler waited, printed "System reset failed"
and panicked, leaving the board hung. Any PSCI reboot reaching BL31 --
the kernel's panic=10 auto-reboot, a clean reboot, an A/B revert -- hit
this.

Reload the counter through the control register (bit 0, guarded by the
0x0a57 key) after enabling the watchdog, and hold the enable asserted
until the reset lands, mirroring the mainline sunxi_wdt driver's restart
sequence. The mmio_write to the config/mode registers needs no key on
this SoC (the kernel binds the sun6i-a31-wdt fallback, key 0).
---
diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
index 148f50e..6d1f46c 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
@@ -18,6 +18,9 @@
 #define SUNXI_WDOG0_CFG_REG		(SUNXI_R_WDOG_BASE + 0x0014)
 #define SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG		(SUNXI_R_WDOG_BASE + 0x0018)

+/* Reload the watchdog counter (bit 0), guarded by the 0x0a57 key. */
+#define SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_RELOAD		((0x0a57 << 1) | 1)
+
 static int sunxi_pwr_domain_on(u_register_t mpidr)
 {
 	sunxi_cpu_on(mpidr);
@@ -59,8 +62,19 @@ static void __dead2 sunxi_system_reset(void)
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CFG_REG, 1);
 	/* Enable the watchdog with the shortest timeout (0.5 seconds) */
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG, (0 << 4) | 1);
-	/* Wait for twice the watchdog timeout before panicking */
-	mdelay(1000);
+	/*
+	 * Enabling the mode register does not start the counter on H616/H618;
+	 * it must be reloaded through the control register (guarded by the
+	 * 0x0a57 key). Without this the watchdog never fires and the reset
+	 * silently fails. This mirrors the mainline sunxi_wdt restart path.
+	 */
+	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_REG, SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_RELOAD);
+
+	/* Hold the watchdog enabled until the reset takes effect. */
+	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < 200; i++) {
+		mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG, (0 << 4) | 1);
+		mdelay(5);
+	}

 	ERROR("PSCI: System reset failed\n");
 	panic();
